  "description": "We aim to urgently replace our original windows due to failure of the windows. We have attempted extensive restoration of the windows but this has not been affective. They are single glazed windows with rotted wooden frames and despite restoration and further work to keep them in good order they are leaking, do not shut and are inadequate for keeping heat in, with water on the internals during winter. Recently rain has penetrated through all the windows to the front and rear of my flat. We plan to replace them with “A”rated traditional casement windows including new Accoya® wood frames. We will retain the design of the windows so that there will be no change to the external appearance of the property.  The new windows will be constructed of hardwood and are to have a white painted finish externally in common with all Bedford Park properties. These windows will improve the look of the house significantly due to being structurally sound and are built to last so will maintain the external look for much longer. As we upgrade the windows we will add double glazed units that meet current thermal requirements as this will not change the look of the windows but will significantly reduced carbon emissions.  With an estimated drop in heating requirement of 30-60%.With climate change moving fast we must all do what we can to reduce our carbon foot print as this will retain the external look in keeping with our grade II listed guidance it should only be a positive.\nAs we have better access to the walls we will review walls for any damage to brickwork or roof and action any repairs that are required. Ensuring that the repair match the original as much as is possible. ",
